  triage:title "am1-removal-ledger.md's own freeze gate remains unmet despite plan-phase-am.md now showing status: complete" ;
  triage:description "QA-AM-END-RECHECK (blocking, req-qa AND arch-qa independently): this branch flipped docs/plans/phase-am/plan-phase-am.md's frontmatter to status: complete, but docs/plans/phase-am/am1-removal-ledger.md -- a required AM.1 deliverable -- still self-declares 'draft' with an unchecked freeze task requiring the accepted AL.9 evidence SHA to be recorded. That evidence already exists in docs/plans/phase-am/am6-closure-proof.md (SHA 6a7e0e0399ef782176e0d20d7d593942154e0598) but was never written back into the ledger. Both reviewers independently ruled this is NOT a duplicate of the already-closed AM2-ENTRY-GATE-SEQUENCING finding (that resolved a different sequencing question about M5 cross-host evidence) -- this is the ledger's own internal bookkeeping gate, separately unmet. Fix: write the accepted AL.9 evidence SHA into am1-removal-ledger.md's freeze section, check the freeze task, and update the ledger's own status line to reflect the accepted freeze." ;
